ects duplicate keys when the attrset is\n              evaluated, causing evaluation failures.","id":"nix/duplicate-attrset-key","kind":"problem","name":"Duplicate attrset key","precision":"very-high","problem.severity":"warning"}},{"id":"nix/shell-injection-in-build-phase","name":"nix/shell-injection-in-build-phase","shortDescription":{"text":"Shell injection in derivation build phase"},"fullDescription":{"text":"An untrusted value (function formal, fetcher result, `getEnv`, `import`) flows into a shell-context attribute (`buildPhase`, `installPhase`, etc.) without being passed through `lib.escapeShellArg`. An attacker who controls the source value can break out of the interpolation and execute arbitrary shell commands during the build."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"error"},"properties":{"tags":["security","external/cwe/cwe-077","external/cwe/cwe-078","supply-chain"],"description":"An untrusted value (function formal, fetcher result,\n              `getEnv`, `import`) flows into a shell-context attribute\n              (`buildPhase`, `installPhase`, etc.) without being\n              passed through `lib.escapeShellArg`. An attacker who\n              controls the source value can break out of the\n              interpolation and execute arbitrary shell commands\n              during the build.","id":"nix/shell-injection-in-build-phase","kind":"problem","name":"Shell injection in derivation build phase","precision":"medium","problem.severity":"error","security-severity":"8.0"}},{"id":"nix/missing-shell-escape","name":"nix/missing-shell-escape","shortDescription":{"text":"Missing shell-escape on derivation interpolation"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A `${expr}` interpolation inside one of `mkDerivation`'s shell-context attributes is not passed through `lib.escapeShellArg` (or an equivalent sanitizer). Defensive escaping is recommended for any value that wasn't explicitly proven safe."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"warning"},"properties":{"tags":["security","external/cwe/cwe-077","external/cwe/cwe-078","maintainability"],"description":"A `${expr}` interpolation inside one of `mkDerivation`'s\n              shell-context attributes is not passed through\n              `lib.escapeShellArg` (or an equivalent sanitizer).\n              Defensive escaping is recommended for any value that\n              wasn't explicitly proven safe.","id":"nix/missing-shell-escape","kind":"problem","name":"Missing shell-escape on derivation interpolation","precision":"low","problem.severity":"warning","security-severity":"6.5"}},{"id":"nix/unpinned-import-fetch","name":"nix/unpinned-import-fetch","shortDescription":{"text":"`import` of unpinned fetcher result"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Importing the result of an unpinned fetcher call downloads and evaluates mutable network-controlled Nix code. An attacker who can tamper with the fetched content can execute arbitrary Nix code during evaluation."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"error"},"properties":{"tags":["security","external/cwe/cwe-829","external/cwe/cwe-094","supply-chain"],"description":"Importing the result of an unpinned fetcher call downloads and\n              evaluates mutable network-controlled Nix code. An attacker who\n              can tamper with the fetched content can execute arbitrary Nix\n              code during evaluation.","id":"nix/unpinned-import-fetch","kind":"problem","name":"`import` of unpinned fetcher result","precision":"high","problem.severity":"error","security-severity":"9.0"}},{"id":"nix/fetch-without-integrity","name":"nix/fetch-without-integrity","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetcher invoked without an integrity hash"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A `fetchTarball`/`fetchurl`/`fetchgit`/`fetchFrom*` call without a `sha256`, `narHash`, or `hash` attribute (or called with a bare URL string) downloads content whose authenticity cannot be verified. An attacker who controls the upstream URL — or any network position in between — can substitute malicious code that will be evaluated by every Nix evaluation."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"error"},"properties":{"tags":["security","external/cwe/cwe-829","external/cwe/cwe-494","supply-chain"],"description":"A `fetchTarball`/`fetchurl`/`fetchgit`/`fetchFrom*` call\n              without a `sha256`, `narHash`, or `hash` attribute (or\n              called with a bare URL string) downloads content whose\n              authenticity cannot be verified. An attacker who controls\n              the upstream URL — or any network position in between —\n              can substitute malicious code that will be evaluated by\n              every Nix evaluation.","id":"nix/fetch-without-integrity","kind":"problem","name":"Fetcher invoked without an integrity hash","precision":"high","problem.severity":"error","security-severity":"7.5"}},{"id":"nix/nix-path-lookup","name":"nix/nix-path-lookup","shortDescription":{"text":"<...>-style search-path lookup"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A `<...>`-style search-path lookup such as `<nixpkgs>` resolves via the ambient `$NIX_PATH`/`builtins.nixPath` search path. That search path differs across machines and over time, making evaluation non-reproducible and allowing unexpected code to be imported."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"warning"},"properties":{"tags":["security","external/cwe/cwe-829","supply-chain","reproducibility"],"description":"A `<...>`-style search-path lookup such as `<nixpkgs>`\n              resolves via the ambient `$NIX_PATH`/`builtins.nixPath`\n              search path. That search path differs across machines and\n              over time, making evaluation non-reproducible and allowing\n              unexpected code to be imported.","id":"nix/nix-path-lookup","kind":"problem","name":"<...>-style search-path lookup","precision":"very-high","problem.severity":"warning","security-severity":"5.0"}},{"id":"nix/unused-binding","name":"nix/unused-binding","shortDescription":{"text":"Unused binding"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A name is defined by a `let`-binding, `rec`-attrset binding, `inherit`, or function parameter, but is never referenced in its lexical scope. Unused bindings make code harder to maintain and may indicate a refactoring error such as a forgotten use site."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"note"},"properties":{"tags":["maintainability","external/cwe/cwe-563"],"description":"A name is defined by a `let`-binding, `rec`-attrset\n              binding, `inherit`, or function parameter, but is never\n              referenced in its lexical scope. Unused bindings make\n              code harder to maintain and may indicate a refactoring\n              error such as a forgotten use site.","id":"nix/unused-binding","kind":"problem","name":"Unused binding","precision":"medium","problem.severity":"recommendation"}},{"id":"nix/rec-attrset-merge","name":"nix/rec-attrset-merge","shortDescription":{"text":"`rec { ... }` merged with `//`"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Merging a recursive attrset with `//` is misleading because references inside the `rec` block resolve only within that block, not against the merged result."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"warning"},"properties":{"tags":["correctness","external/cwe/cwe-665","maintainability"],"description":"Merging a recursive attrset with `//` is misleading because\n              references inside the `rec` block resolve only within that\n              block, not against the merged result.","id":"nix/rec-attrset-merge","kind":"problem","name":"`rec { ... }` merged with `//`","precision":"high","problem.severity":"warning"}},{"id":"nix/space-in-flag-string","name":"nix/space-in-flag-string","shortDescription":{"text":"Whitespace inside a flag-list string literal"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A literal string inside `cmakeFlags`/`mesonFlags`/`configureFlags`/`makeFlags` (and similar argv-style attributes) that contains embedded whitespace is word-split by nixpkgs' build wrapper into multiple argv entries, silently changing the invoked command line."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"error"},"properties":{"tags":["correctness","external/cwe/cwe-078","maintainability"],"description":"A literal string inside `cmakeFlags`/`mesonFlags`/`configureFlags`/`makeFlags`\n              (and similar argv-style attributes) that contains embedded whitespace is\n              word-split by nixpkgs' build wrapper into\n              multiple argv entries, silently changing the invoked command line.","id":"nix/space-in-flag-string","kind":"problem","name":"Whitespace inside a flag-list string literal","precision":"very-high","problem.severity":"error","security-severity":"4.0"}},{"id":"nix/builtins-get-env","name":"nix/builtins-get-env","shortDescription":{"text":"Use of `builtins.getEnv`"},"fullDescription":{"text":"`builtins.getEnv` reads the host environment during evaluation. That is impure, behaves differently under `--pure-eval`, and can leak host state into derivation hashes and outputs."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"warning"},"properties":{"tags":["reliability","external/cwe/cwe-807","impurity"],"description":"`builtins.getEnv` reads the host environment during evaluation. That is impure,\n              behaves differently under `--pure-eval`, and can leak host state into derivation\n              hashes and outputs.","id":"nix/builtins-get-env","kind":"problem","name":"Use of `builtins.getEnv`","precision":"high","problem.severity":"warning","security-severity":"3.5"}},{"id":"nix/legacy-let-attrset","name":"nix/legacy-let-attrset","shortDescription":{"text":"Deprecated legacy `let { … }` attrset syntax"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The legacy `let { body = ...; }` attrset form is deprecated and supported only for backwards compatibility. Prefer `let ... in ...` instead."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"warning"},"properties":{"tags":["maintainability","external/cwe/cwe-477","deprecated"],"description":"The legacy `let { body = ...; }` attrset form is deprecated\n              and supported only for backwards compatibility. Prefer\n              `let ... in ...` instead.","id":"nix/legacy-let-attrset","kind":"problem","name":"Deprecated legacy `let { … }` attrset syntax","precision":"very-high","problem.severity":"warning"}},{"id":"nix/deprecated-uri-literal","name":"nix/deprecated-uri-literal","shortDescription":{"text":"Deprecated bare URI literal"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A bare (unquoted) URI literal such as `https://example.com` is deprecated by Nix RFC 45 and is scheduled for removal from the language. Quote the URI as a string literal instead."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"warning"},"properties":{"tags":["maintainability","external/cwe/cwe-477","deprecated"],"description":"A bare (unquoted) URI literal such as `https://example.com`\n              is deprecated by Nix RFC 45 and is scheduled for removal from\n              the language. Quote the URI as a string literal instead.","id":"nix/deprecated-uri-literal","kind":"problem","name":"Deprecated bare URI literal","precision":"very-high","problem.severity":"warning"}}]},"extensions":[{"name":"jamiemagee/nix-queries","semanticVersion":"0.1.0+318f6a35b604cdf3229b71bc44adec1e1b261f2e","locations":[{"uri":"file:///home/jamie/src/code/codeql-nix/ql/src/","description":{"text":"The QL pack root directory."},"properties":{"tags":["CodeQL/LocalPackRoot"]}},{"uri":"file:///home/jamie/src/code/codeql-nix/ql/src/qlpack.yml","description":{"text":"The QL pack definition file."},"properties":{"tags":["CodeQL/LocalPackDefinitionFile"]}}]}]},"invocations":[{"toolExecutionNotifications":[{"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"pkgs/development/mobile/androidenv/update.rb","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%","index":10318}}}],"message":{"text":""},"level":"none","descriptor":{"id":"rb/baseline/expected-extracted-files","index":0},"properties":{"form